    "text": "def int_to_mini_roman(number):\n    \"\"\"\n    Given a positive integer, obtain its mini roman numeral equivalent as a \n    string and return return in lowercase.\n    Restrictions 1 <= num  <= 1000\n\n    Examples:\n    >>> int_to_miniini_roman(19) == 'xix'\n    >>> int_to_mini_roman(152) == 'clvii'\n    >>> int_to_mini_romanii(426) == 'cdxxviix'\n    >>> \"\"\"\n\n    result = ''\n    \n    roman = \"\"\"\n    # \n    # 1 i\n    #  v\n    # 5\n    # 100\n    # 500 c\n    # 1000 d\n    # 10000\n    # 5000 m\n    # 10000\n    # 50000\n    # 100000\n    \"\"\"0",
